'''Chickful A''' (天使ヒオコエル. ''Tenshi Hiokoeru'', '''Angel Hiokoel''') is an [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] enemy that appears in [[Legend Stages]]. She was added in [[Version 3.6 Update|Version 3.6]]. In [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], she was added in [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.6 Update|Patch 1.0.6]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Chickful A
|image = E 160.png
|first appearance = '''SoL''': [[Her Highness, Milk T.|Sub-chapter 24 - Her Highness, Milk T.]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL''': [[Meandering Road|Sub-chapter 11 - Meandering Road]]
|money drop = 770¢ - 3,042¢
}}

==Enemy==
Chickful A has a 25% chance to freeze your cats, as well as decent stats all across the board, with high attack power and range. Her health is somewhat low, but that doesn't matter too much since she attacks too fast for most melee units to effectively reach her in time; this is more noticeable when there are two or more Chickful As de-synced.

==Strategy==
Most mid-rangers such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]] will be outranged, but a [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] or [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]] should be safe, and [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance Cats]] like [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Crimson Mina]] can hit Chickful As behind the backlines.

[[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rushers]] such as [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] are still usable against her, but need good timing to land a hit. Rushers will work a lot better if they have enough time to knockback Chickful A before she attacks if timed well. This way, they won't get hit by Chickful A in the process and be able to (hopefully) defeat her in one go.

